messages:
ada: opened a quick PR for the 'Starlit' dark theme — main asks: increase chart label contrast, adjust code syntax so strings are warmer, and add keyboard-friendly focus for compact controls. screenshots in PR.

ben: loading the images now. first look: panel dividers disappear in OLED variant. recommend a 1px semi-opaque separator on true-black.

claire: flag: legend text at 11px is hard to read on small cards. bump to 13px and use --text-primary instead of muted.

tariq: colorblind note: the gradient we're using for token heatmap (purple->green) collides in protanopia. suggest single-hue sequential (teal->navy) or amber ramp.

eva: code blocks: keywords and types are too similar. proposed mapping: keyword #cfa8ff, string #ffb47a, function #7fbfff. makes scanning easier. also add slightly darker inline-code bg: rgba(0,0,0,0.25).

ada: quick CSS vars I'm trying in the branch:

```css
:root {
  --bg-900: #07090b;
  --panel-800: #0e1113;
  --text-primary: #e8eef4;
  --muted: #98a4ab;
  --accent: #7fbfff;
}
```

ben: UX nit: focus ring on icon-only buttons is barely visible. make it 3px and use a slightly desaturated accent so it doesn't glare.

claire: copy suggestion: change toggle label from "Enable dark mode" to "Dark theme" and add tooltip: "Optimized for low-glare viewing and night work". shorter and consistent with settings.

tariq: charts: on hover add a small inner glow rather than increasing stroke width to keep default clean. `filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.6));` could work.

eva: I'll run a quick CVD sim after you push the palette. ping me @eva and I'll attach the images. :mag:

design-bot: PR #981 created by ada (branch/starlit-theme). CI: visual diffs pending (3 images).

ada: thanks all — updating PR to: bump legend/kpi text sizes, swap heatmap to sequential teal, update syntax tokens, OLED separators, and focus ring change. will add accessibility checklist to the PR description. merging once visuals are green :sparkles:
